From bfd8ab9f691561e1f2e75e6537bc4f58cec9a910 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stanislav Bardyuk <6258615+kodlan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 19:07:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net_ib: Order CTS nreqs load after the idx check

Problem: ncclIbIsend checks slots[0].idx and then loads slots[0].nreqs
from the CTS fifo element written by the peer's NIC. Nothing orders the
second load after the first; the existing seq_cst fence comes after both.
On weakly ordered CPUs (AArch64, POWER) the nreqs load can be satisfied
before the idx load and return the slot's previous-round value. Slots are
never cleared, so a stale larger value makes the per-slot idx wait loop
spin forever and hangs the proxy thread; a stale smaller value posts too
few RDMA writes.

Solution: add an acquire fence between the idx check and the nreqs load.
It compiles to nothing on x86 and to one dmb ishld on AArch64, only on
the path where the CTS has arrived. The existing fence stays to order the
per-slot idx waits against the field loads that follow.

Limitations: verified by build, clang-format, nccl-tests on x86, and by
inspecting the aarch64 code of an extract of the loop; the hang itself
was not reproduced (no Arm host with an RDMA NIC available).

Fixes #1983

Signed-off-by: Stanislav Bardyuk <6258615+kodlan@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/transport/net_ib/p2p.cc | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/transport/net_ib/p2p.cc b/src/transport/net_ib/p2p.cc
index fadf363..5ee5455 100644
--- a/src/transport/net_ib/p2p.cc
+++ b/src/transport/net_ib/p2p.cc
@@ -283,6 +283,8 @@ ncclResult_t ncclIbIsend(void* sendComm, void* data, size_t size, int tag, void*
     *request = NULL;
     return ncclSuccess;
   }
+  // Order the nreqs load after the idx load above; on weakly ordered CPUs it could otherwise return a stale value.
+  std::atomic_thread_fence(std::memory_order_acquire);
   nreqs = slots[0].nreqs;
   // Wait until all data has arrived
   for (int r = 1; r < nreqs; r++) {
-- 
